{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The reason for <b>And YHWH spoke to Moses, saying:</b> Because these commandments are binding upon all Israel, and there is no foreigner among them, therefore it is written at the beginning, \"to all the congregation of Israel.\" Now He begins to mention the punishment for harlotry, upon everyone who dwells in the Land, whether native or resident stranger. And He begins with the most severe of them all, namely one who gives of his seed to Molech, and the meaning is to lie with an idolatress."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:16.902875309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}